Section: utils
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: Live-updating nvidia-smi with a minimal terminal UI
 nvidia-smi-live re-renders every GPU on a timer — utilization, VRAM,
 temperature, power and fan — as a minimal terminal UI, with a per-process
 memory table laid out like nvidia-smi's. It also exports the same snapshot
 as JSON, NDJSON or a Prometheus textfile.
 .
 The binary is under 400 KB and links only libc and libgcc_s. It loads
 libnvidia-ml.so.1 from the NVIDIA driver at runtime via dlopen. It needs a
 working NVIDIA driver to do anything useful; there is no driver dependency
 to declare, because
 the driver packages differ per vendor and generation. It is built against
 glibc 2.35, so it needs Debian 12 (bookworm) or newer, or Ubuntu 22.04 or
 newer.
